Aerie-Purpose: Add the Tab layout row to the Sidebar section of Settings and let the settings page write the layout pref.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/resources/settings (appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.ts, appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.html.ts, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings (settings_localized_strings_provider.cc), chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private (prefs_util.cc)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #186. settings-aerie-layout-row is a Lit element in the overlay (appearance_page/aerie_layout_row.*): a radio group on aerie.sidebar.layout with Sidebar, Horizontal (two rows) and Horizontal (one row). The pref name is a string literal in the allowlist, as for the other Aerie prefs, and a test compares it with aerie_sidebar::kLayoutPref.

--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc
@@ -517,7 +517,8 @@
   (*s_allowlist)["aerie.sidebar.side"] = settings_api::PrefType::kString;
   // Aerie: the sidebar's width and shown state (issue #177). The names are
   // aerie_sidebar::kWidthPref and kVisiblePref; a test compares them. The
-  // layout pref is not here until issue #186 builds the second layout.
+  // layout pref is the next entry (issue #186); aerie_sidebar::kLayoutPref.
+  (*s_allowlist)["aerie.sidebar.layout"] = settings_api::PrefType::kString;
   (*s_allowlist)["aerie.sidebar.width"] = settings_api::PrefType::kNumber;
   (*s_allowlist)["aerie.sidebar.visible"] = settings_api::PrefType::kBoolean;
 
